//
// Scoped Verilator lint waivers for the Verilator simulation lane. Each
// waiver is scoped to one rule and one file/instance, with a comment
// explaining why - see openspec/changes/verilator-sim-flow/design.md
// (Risks: "CVA6/Cheshire RTL trips Verilator") for the policy this follows.
// Do NOT add a blanket `-Wno-*` or an unscoped `lint_off` here.

`verilator_config

// axi_llc_tag_store.sv zero-initializes a struct containing an enum member
// via `'{default: '0}` - a widespread, harmless SystemVerilog idiom for
// "zero this struct", not an actual invalid enum value. Verilator's
// ENUMVALUE check (IEEE 1800-2023 6.19.3, implicit bit->enum conversion)
// flags it at error severity by default. Upstream (pulp-platform/axi_llc),
// not modified here per the project's dependency strategy (fork only if it
// actively blocks us - this doesn't; it's an inert lint waiver).
lint_off -rule ENUMVALUE -file "*axi_llc_tag_store.sv"
